faces are defined but not used\n2. **Validation Only**: Rule validation exists but there are no rules to validate\n3. **No Simulation Engine**: There is NO `src/lib/simulation.ts` file\n4. **No Core Logic**: No neighbor counting, no rule application, no grid evolution\n5. **No Implementation**: The simulation is entirely planned but not written\n\n## What Needs to Be Implemented\n\nAccording to the specs, the simulation engine needs:\n\n1. **Core Game of Life Rules** (`src/lib/simulation.ts` - NOT CREATED)\n   - RuleSet with born/survive arrays\n   - Conway's rules: born=[3], survive=[2,3]\n   - Neighbor counting with Moore neighborhood (8 cells)\n   - Toroidal boundary handling (wrap edges with modulo)\n   - Age tracking (increment on survival, 1 for birth)\n   - Double-buffer pattern for state updates\n\n2. **Performance Optimizations**\n   - React ref for grid state (to avoid re-renders)\n   - Precomputed neighbor offset array\n   - requestAnimationFrame with delta time\n   - Speed ref to avoid state dependency\n\n3. **Generation Counter**\n   - Track generation number\n   - Trigger React render on generation change\n\n4. **Grid Resizing**\n   - Support three sizes: 20×30, 40×50, 60×80\n   - Clear and reset when dimensions change\n\n5. **Birth Statistics**\n   - Count born cells\n   - Track average row position for audio mapping\n\n## Package.json Analysis\n\n- **Keywords**: Include \"game-of-life\" and \"cellular-automaton\"\n- **Description**: \"Conway's Game of Life - A strategic cellular automaton puzzle game\"\n- **Dependencies**: No game-of-life related packages (only React and React-DOM)\n- **DevDependencies**: Testing libraries (Vitest, Testing Library) but no simulation libraries\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe codebase is in the **very early planning stage**:\n- Project structure is set up\n- Types are defined\n- Validation utilities exist for future use\n- Specs and implementation plan are detailed\n- **But NO actual simulation code exists yet**\n\nThe simulation engine must be built from scratch as planned in `src/lib/simulation.ts` according to the detailed specification in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/simulation-engine.md`.\n</task_result>","title":"Search for simulation code","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39e35ad90ffeMi73L38K1Opov9","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771167175276,"end":1771167235434}}}}
